# CODEOWNERS: required reviewers for supply-chain-sensitive paths
# (Phase 4, blocker 4).
#
# This file has an effect ONLY where GitHub is configured to require it:
# "Require review from Code Owners" on a rule that covers `main`. Set it in
# repo Settings -> Rules, or in the classic Settings -> Branches -> branch
# protection. This repo currently
# allows direct pushes to `main` by design. So today this file only records
# ownership, and it starts to gate changes when that setting is turned on.
# It does not block a direct push.
#
# .github/** is the entire publish path: every workflow, the planner, and
# the build/push script. images.yaml is the catalog that decides what is
# built, from which base image, and with which tags. A change to either is as
# sensitive as a change to the images themselves.
.github/**    @raubreywhite
images.yaml   @raubreywhite
